{"path":"types/is_corresponding_member","title":"std::is_corresponding_member","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>is_corresponding_member","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/is_corresponding_member","section":"types","kind":"page","summary":"Determines whether mp and mq refer corresponding members in the common initial sequence of S1 and S2. The program is ill-formed if either S1 or S2 is an incomplete type.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/type_traits\">&lt;type_traits&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> S1, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> S2, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> M1, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> M2 <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> is_corresponding_member<span class=\"br0\">(</span> M1 S1<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> mp, M2 S2<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> mq <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Determines whether <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">mp</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">mq</span></code> refer corresponding members in the <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/data_members#Standard-layout\">common initial sequence</a> of <code>S1</code> and <code>S2</code>. The program is ill-formed if either <code>S1</code> or <code>S2</code> is an <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/type#Incomplete_type\">incomplete type</a>.\n</p><p>If either <code>S1</code> or <code>S2</code> is not a <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/StandardLayoutType\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">StandardLayoutType</em></a>, or either <code>M1</code> or <code>M2</code> is not an object type, or either <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">mp</span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">mq</span></code> is equal to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">nullptr</span></code>, the result is always <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> mp, mq\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointers-to-member to detect\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">mp</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">mq</span></code> refer corresponding members in the common initial sequence of <code>S1</code> and <code>S2</code>, otherwise <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">false</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The type of a pointer-to-member expression <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>S<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">m</span></span></code> is not always <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">M S<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span></span></code>, where <code>m</code> is of type <code>M</code>, because <code>m</code> may be a member inherited from a base class of <code>S</code>. The template arguments can be specified in order to avoid potentially surprising results.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;type_traits&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> Foo\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> x<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> d<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> Bar\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> y<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> z<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> Baz <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> Foo, Bar <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// not standard-layout</span>\n&nbsp;\nstatic_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_same\"><span class=\"kw592\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_same_v</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>decltype<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Baz<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">x</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> Foo<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">true</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_same\"><span class=\"kw592\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_same_v</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>decltype<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Baz<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">y</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> Bar<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">true</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_corresponding_member</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Foo<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">x</span>, <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Bar<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">y</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">true</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_corresponding_member</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Foo<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">d</span>, <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Bar<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">z</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">true</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_corresponding_member</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Baz<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">x</span>, <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Baz<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">y</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">true</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_corresponding_member</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Baz, Baz, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span>, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Baz<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">x</span>, <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>Baz<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">y</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">false</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_standard_layout\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_standard_layout</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if a type is a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/data_members#Standard-layout\">standard-layout</a> type <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_layout_compatible\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_layout_compatible</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   checks if two types are <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/data_members#Standard_layout\"><i>layout-compatible</i></a>  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_member_object_pointer\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_member_object_pointer</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if a type is a non-static member object pointer <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"types","title":"Type support (basic types, RTTI)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::is_corresponding_member","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++20. Determines whether mp and mq refer corresponding members in the common initial sequence of S1 and S2."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"mp, mq"},{"label":"Return value","note":"true if mp and mq refer corresponding members in the common initial sequence of S1 and S2, otherwise false."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The type of a pointer-to-member expression &S::m is not always M S::*, where m is of type M, because m may be a member inherited from a base class of S."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"is_standard_layout","note":"checks if a type is a standard-layout type"},{"label":"is_layout_compatible","note":"checks if two types are layout-compatible"},{"label":"is_member_object_pointer","note":"checks if a type is a non-static member object pointer"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":264,"codeBlockCount":1}
